; FACTORIAL.LGO - recursion you can watch, step by step
;
; 5! (five factorial) is 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1. A recursive definition says
; the same thing: the factorial of N is N times the factorial of N - 1,
; and the factorial of 0 is 1.
;
; Try the debugger:
;   1. Click in the margin next to the line "if :n = 0 [output 1]".
;   2. Press F5. The program stops there.
;   3. Open Call Stack: one FACTORIAL is waiting inside another.
;   4. Click an older frame to see its own :n in Variables.
;   5. Press F5 to continue, or F11 to take one step at a time.

to factorial :n
  if :n = 0 [output 1]
  output :n * factorial :n - 1
end

for [i 0 10] [print (sentence :i "! "= factorial :i)]
